Effects
Sometimes, instead of calculating a new value that will dynamically change when andependency changes, we just want to perform some “unrelated” action whenever a signal changes its values. For example, we might want to send an HTTP request that
would track a user’s action or maybe set a FormControl’s value based on some signal or something else.
Signal effects are always asynchronous.This means that if during one function execution the value of a signal that an effect watches changes several times, we will receive only the last one and perform the effect’s logic on it once
Similar to the inject function, we can only register effects in contexts where the DI tree is available.
Եթե առանձին մեթոդի մեջ է գրվում,պետք է փոխանցել կոմպոնենտի ինջեկտորի ռեֆերենսը՝ - այս մասը մի հատ ուրիշ տեղ էլ կարդալ, որովհետև հիմա առանց constructor-ում էլ արեցի եղավՃ - էջ 144
private readonly injector = inject(Injector);
someMethod() {
 effect(() => {
console.log(this.someSignal())
 }, {injector: this.injector});
}

